{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThis workstream has 19 remediation leaves, 273 distinct retired per-file source tickets, and 258 distinct present execution paths in reconciler unit tests and fixtures at `origin/main@e539e4a65d3e7451ca3dbc4b754ba4a2370cc3cc`. 15 historical source paths have no present current target. The one source-free current path is Natant's copied rich-text seam; its retired source remains linked to Dialectal. This story makes no repository edits. Grouped-commit `file_impact` may list sibling paths for completion precheck; those union entries do not create another Scope owner or migration source.\n\n## Plan\n- Complete all 19 leaves using each leaf's exact Scope, behavior contracts, and recorded checks. Each leaf edits only allowlisted prose, preserves runtime strings, assertions, directives, and behavior-bearing test contracts, obtains a non-author per-block semantic and bloat TSV, passes Gerrit's `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` with zero unresolved comments, and closes only after its merged revision and completion verification are recorded. Record a local `make verify` pass where required; older session-authorized comment-only leaves may instead record explicit local-full delegation to Gerrit's Verified gate.\n- Derive two sorted TSVs from live children, their net-active `replacement -supersedes-> retired source` links, current Scope, and Git path evidence. Preserve immutable source ticket ID and historical path even when the file moved, was copied, or was deleted.\n- Historical migration TSV (273 rows): `source_id<TAB>source_alias<TAB>historical_source_path<TAB>historical_replacement_leaf<TAB>disposition<TAB>verified_current_path_or_blank<TAB>current_action_leaf_or_blank<TAB>git_or_ticket_evidence`. A deleted source has no current path; a copied target keeps its original supersedes link.\n- Current execution TSV (258 rows): `current_path<TAB>execution_leaf_alias<TAB>source_count<TAB>retired_source_alias_or_blank<TAB>copy_source_alias_or_blank<TAB>scope_evidence<TAB>pinned_main`. Count each present path once under its actual Scope owner. Exactly 1 current paths have `source_count=0`; 257 directly linked paths have `source_count=1`.\n- Store both final TSVs in a dedicated `session_log` linked `relates_to` this story. At completion, record the final main SHA, row counts, both SHA-256 values, leaf merged commits, local or Gerrit verification results, and non-author reviewer-log or receipt IDs. The e539 working drafts have broader crosswalk columns and SHA-256 `4850d561803633176c06fb6c48d2de0292e067bcff36c35d5268a786d1eefe9b` and `8b2a26fe874deed9bb06592945cb1aa4ea80bedef30cbe3bb9b84a454b05525e`; verify live Scope and transform them to the final schema after the remaining merges. Final placeholders: `<FINAL_MAIN_SHA>`, `<MIGRATION_TSV_SHA256>`, `<EXECUTION_TSV_SHA256>`, and `<STORY_SESSION_LOG_ALIAS>`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All 19 child leaves are closed after their Gerrit changes merge and completion checks pass.\n- [ ] The migration TSV contains exactly 273 rows with 273 distinct retired source IDs and historical paths. Every retired source has exactly one net-active replacement leaf.\n- [ ] Every migration row records its historical path, disposition, evidence, and current path or an explicit no-current-path reason. The 15 source paths without current targets remain in this historical inventory.\n- [ ] The execution TSV contains exactly 258 rows with 258 distinct present paths at the final main SHA, each with exactly one Scope owner or an explicitly identified copied-follow-up owner.\n- [ ] Exactly 257 execution rows have `source_count=1` and 1 have `source_count=0`. Source-free rows are explained by the recorded additions or copied-target lineage.\n- [ ] The inventories count unique Scope-owned paths; grouped-commit `file_impact` union entries remain contextual and do not inflate source or current-path counts.\n- [ ] Every migrated Scope constraint and consumer contract has a non-author `semantic-preservation=PASS` row with immutable before/final citations; every edited prose block has non-author `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every required leaf verification command exits 0 at its cited commit. A legacy local-full waiver is identified explicitly and paired with Gerrit `Verified +1`; it is not reported as a local pass. Each leaf trail records its Gerrit Change-Id, `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, zero unresolved comments, `MERGED` status, and exact merged SHA reachable from final main.\n- [ ] The story log records each leaf's merged commit, command result, and reviewer-log or per-block receipt ID. The completion comment cites that log and both final TSV row counts and SHA-256 values.\n\n## Completion boundary\nClose this story only after every child is closed and both final inventories pass these checks at `<FINAL_MAIN_SHA>`.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792815297054939071,"uuid":"7fc328cb-9af9-4220-8b72-9f7ef9e75131"}